      "key": "chen2016quickest",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "scope": "contextual scope attribution",
      "file": "sections/narrative_protocol.tex",
      "line": 33,
      "before": "The published physical comparator is Chen \\emph{et al.}'s persistent single-line quickest-change detector \\cite{chen2016quickest}. Its reduced-network covariance is marginalized to the observed PMU subset after inversion. Parallel CUSUM statistics stop at the first threshold crossing and select a line. Our declared F01 adapter uses nonoverlapping angle increments at 15 Hz, a startup-only scale/drift estimate and the fixed nominal line catalog. Its white-injection/DC assumptions do not describe all F01 instrumental effects. We preserve both matched-law implementation checks and F01 mismatch failures; no ARL guarantee is transferred to colored noise.",
      "after": "The published physical comparator is Chen \\emph{et al.}'s persistent-line quickest-change detector \\cite{chen2016quickest}, which considers single- and double-line outages. Our declared F01 adapter restricts its fixed nominal catalog to single-line hypotheses. Its reduced-network covariance is marginalized to the observed PMU subset after inversion. Parallel CUSUM statistics stop at the first threshold crossing and select a line. The adapter uses nonoverlapping angle increments at 15 Hz and a startup-only scale/drift estimate. Its white-injection/DC assumptions do not describe all F01 instrumental effects. We preserve both matched-law implementation checks and F01 mismatch failures; no ARL guarantee is transferred to colored noise.",
      "source_audit_trace": ".aris/traces/citation-audit/20261101_run01/chen2016quickest.md",
      "evidence_urls": [
